The four countries with the strongest agriculture are Brazil, [Argentina](/wiki/Argentina "Argentina"), Chile and [Colombia](/wiki/Colombia "Colombia"). Currently:

* Brazil is the world's largest producer of [sugarcane](/wiki/Sugarcane "Sugarcane"), [soy](/wiki/Soy "Soy"), coffee, orange, [guaraná](/wiki/Guaran%C3%A1 "Guaraná"), [açaí](/wiki/A%C3%A7a%C3%AD "Açaí") and [Brazil nut](/wiki/Brazil_nut "Brazil nut"); is one of the top 5 producers of [maize](/wiki/Maize "Maize"), [papaya](/wiki/Papaya "Papaya"), tobacco, [pineapple](/wiki/Pineapple "Pineapple"), banana, cotton, [beans](/wiki/Beans "Beans"), [coconut](/wiki/Coconut "Coconut"), [watermelon](/wiki/Watermelon "Watermelon"), lemon and [yerba mate](/wiki/Yerba_mate "Yerba mate"); is one of the top 10 world producers of [cocoa](/wiki/Cocoa_bean "Cocoa bean"), [cashew](/wiki/Cashew "Cashew"), [avocado](/wiki/Avocado "Avocado"), [tangerine](/wiki/Tangerine "Tangerine"), [persimmon](/wiki/Persimmon "Persimmon"), [mango](/wiki/Mango "Mango"), [guava](/wiki/Guava "Guava"), rice, [oat](/wiki/Oat "Oat"), [sorghum](/wiki/Sorghum "Sorghum") and tomato; and is one of the top 15 world producers of grape, apple, melon, peanut, [fig](/wiki/Fig "Fig"), [peach](/wiki/Peach "Peach"), onion, [palm oil](/wiki/Palm_oil "Palm oil") and [natural rubber](/wiki/Natural_rubber "Natural rubber");
* Argentina is the world's largest producer of [yerba mate](/wiki/Yerba_mate "Yerba mate"); is one of the five largest producers in the world of [soy](/wiki/Soy "Soy"), maize, [sunflower seed](/wiki/Sunflower_seed "Sunflower seed"), lemon and pear, one of the 10 largest producers in the world of [barley](/wiki/Barley "Barley"), grape, [artichoke](/wiki/Artichoke "Artichoke"), tobacco and cotton, and one of the 15 largest producers in the world of wheat, [oat](/wiki/Oat "Oat"), [chickpea](/wiki/Chickpea "Chickpea"), [sugarcane](/wiki/Sugarcane "Sugarcane"), [sorghum](/wiki/Sorghum "Sorghum") and [grapefruit](/wiki/Grapefruit "Grapefruit");
